{
  "$README": "FROZEN. This is a witness, not a fixture you maintain. It records the wire format a SHIPPED build wrote into a user's ~/.mdpro/config.json, and WI8-G (src-tauri/src/models/preferences_wi8_tests.rs) asserts that today's types still recover every value in it. NEVER EDIT THIS FILE IN THE SAME COMMIT AS A TYPE CHANGE. ADR-0031 declines serde(deny_unknown_fields), so a renamed wire key on a real user's file is silently ignored, serde(default) manufactures a replacement, and the user's value is destroyed with no error raised at any layer. Regenerating this file to get back to green destroys the only witness the third party -- every config.json already on disk -- has. The two legitimate ways back to green are a serde(alias = \"oldName\") or a written migration. A new shipped format gets preferences-shipped-v2.json added BESIDE this one, never an edit to v1. HOW IT WAS BUILT: today's complete key set minus keyboardShortcuts.viewSource, keyboardShortcuts.viewWysiwyg and markdown.autoReformatTablesOnSave, which ADR-0031 step 4 (WI-5) added to the Rust struct in this effort and which therefore never reached a shipped config.json. WI8-G deliberately TOLERATES keys the round trip adds (a new field must not turn a frozen witness red) and asserts only the two directions that mean data loss. Every value is non-default on purpose, so a discarded value cannot coincide with the default that replaces it; the keyboardShortcuts values are synthetic ('Shipped+<wireName>') for that reason. RULE: a '$'-prefixed key is a sibling annotation, skipped by the recursion.",
